BManx2000 wrote:

> Is it possible to disable the "travel" command that happens when you
> click on a square with the mouse? Since I use the windows version, I
> do use the mouse a bit, and the occasional errant click will send me
> somewhere I didn't want to go. Disbaling "travel" in the options only
> disables the travel command when you press "_" (why would you want to
> do that?).

Actually, disabling the "travel" option will restrict movement by
clicking the cursor to just one square.

This is not as the Guidebook tells you, indeed. The Guidebook says:

travel
    Allow the travel command (default on). Turning this option off
    will prevent the game from attempting unintended moves if you
    make inadvertent mouse clicks on the map window.

which suggests that there should be no movement at all, not even the one
move you currently make.

Note that in the tty version (nethack.exe), there is another option:

mouse_support
    Allow use of the mouse for input and travel.


